A||||1||Neal||Plugging Cam & Crank Sensor Holes on 3.4||||5||
Z||000000||Neal||09-30-2001||01:57 PM||||Well im needing some advice here.  I have the 3.4 block ready to assmeble but it came without the cam & crank sensors, Ive tried a few frost plugs and they just arent the right size.  So how do i plug the holes?  ||||reg||5
Z||000001||fierosound||09-30-2001||08:58 PM||||GM has to correct size plugs (they are non-standard of course)<P>PN# 9421749 and PN# 94033681 $6 and change<P>Depending on your block, you may also need a plug on top of the block, just in front of the intake manifold.  I believe it's a 1/2" (12mm) or so.  Be sure to check how your timing cover and water pump fit to the front of the block.  As you remember, I had to block a coolant bypass hole in the timing cover, as there was no corresponding passage in the 3.4L block, and water poured out.<P>Make sure the holes are clean & deoiled.  I put a film of epoxy on the plugs, prior to pressing them in - leakfree and permanent.<p>[This message has been edited by fierosound (edited 09-30-2001).]||||reg||1
